# Optional. Copy to .env ("cp .env.example .env") only if you need to
# override something; Compose reads .env from this directory
# automatically. .env is gitignored because these are host-specific
# values, not repo content.

# The Docker network the ingress reverse proxy is attached to. This
# container joins it so the proxy can reach it as
# patrimonioabierto_web:80.
#
# Only needed if that network is not called "ingress" on your host, which
# is common: a network declared inside another stack's compose file gets
# that stack's Compose project name as a prefix, so it can end up called
# something long and unrelated. Find the real name with:
#
#   docker network ls
#
# and confirm it is the right one by checking the proxy is on it:
#
#   docker network inspect <name> --format '{{range .Containers}}{{.Name}} {{end}}'
#
# Compose only looks this network up (external: true) and never creates
# it, so the name has to match exactly - a wrong one fails the deploy
# rather than starting anything.
#INGRESS_NETWORK=
